From 5a27721cbafcad7578b5640a6b4931e35347b83f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:17:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] feat(api): paginate the list endpoints with pageToken
 and nextPageToken

The list endpoints returned at most `limit` items with no way to fetch
the rest, although the OpenAPI document already promised a
nextPageToken. GET /api/v1/inference-services and GET /api/v1/resources
now accept pageToken and return nextPageToken when more items match,
backed by the signed registry tokens: a token only works for the tenant
and the filters it was issued for (namespace, plus kind on /resources),
the limit may change between pages, and malformed, modified or foreign
tokens are rejected with a 400 error envelope. An empty pageToken starts
at the first page. /resources without kind still returns an empty list,
so a pageToken there is rejected too.

The OpenAPI document gains the pageToken parameter, the count field, the
ordering rule, and the GET /api/v1/resources operation, which the
gateway already proxies but which was never documented.
